    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1135">

                <pb facs="1379" n="1361" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.78/7–3046</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-02T18:00:00-04:00">August 2, 1946—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>320. Urtel 382 July 30. July–Aug flour quota 152,000 cwt fully licensed. Venez
                    importers and American exporters responsible for purchase and shipment. Exports
                    against July–Aug quota may continue leave US through Sept as licenses valid 60
                    days after issuance. <pb facs="1380" n="1362" xml:id="pg1362"/> Improbable large
                    proportion of July–Aug quota will arrive before mid Aug.<anchor n="87"
                        xml:id="d1135-f1"/></p>
                <p>Price ceiling on flour without price ceiling on wheat has created anomalous
                    situation where mills reluctant sell flour. For your confidential info this
                    expected be cleared up shortly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1135-f1" n="87" xml:id="d1135-f1-content">
                <p>In airgram 254, August 22, 1946, to Caracas, the Department indicated that the
                    Department of Agriculture had authorized export of 178,000 cwts of flour to
                    Venezuela for September and October (102.78/8–2246).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
